{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     topnav — the site bar. Marketing, blog, docs, listings, pages.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Composed entirely from chrome/ primitives and NSDS classes; this file
     contributes no markup of its own beyond the arrangement. That is the
     intent — when the training header arrives it is this file plus
     `.ns-pathpick` in the brand slot, not a fork of it.

     Read `assets/css/namaste-ui.css` § navbar for the three decisions the
     shape below follows. In short: state is aria-expanded / aria-current and
     never a class; the bar is solid and never blurred; the current page gets
     a 2px underline and never a filled pill.

     RESPONSIVE — one breakpoint, at lg (64rem / 1024px). Above it the link
     row; below it the hamburger. NSDS's navbar.css does all of it: it hides
     .ns-topnav__links and .ns-topnav__auth, shows .ns-burger, drops the brand
     tagline, and lifts every control in the bar to the 44px thumb floor in
     one line by raising --_control-h. The theme sets no media queries.

     WITH JAVASCRIPT OFF the links, brand and member buttons are all real
     elements, and the current page is still underlined — Ghost computes
     aria-current server-side. Only the sheet and the theme switch go quiet,
     and the footer repeats the navigation so nothing becomes unreachable.

     PARAMETERS
       tagline   passed through to chrome/brand
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<nav class="ns-topnav" aria-label="{{t "Main"}}" data-ns-scrolled>
    {{!-- __inner width-caps the bar's contents so the brand sits exactly
          above a page's first column. NSDS's default bar is fluid; this site
          is width-capped, so the contained variant is the right one. --}}
    <div class="ns-topnav__inner">

        {{> "chrome/brand" tagline=tagline}}

        {{navigation}}

        <div class="ns-topnav__actions">
            {{> "chrome/search"}}
            {{> "chrome/theme-switch"}}

            <div class="ns-topnav__auth">
                {{> "chrome/members" size="sm"}}
            </div>

            {{> "chrome/burger" sheet="site-nav"}}
        </div>

    </div>
</nav>
